# InterviewIQ AI: FastAPI Backend Prompt Pack

Six sequential prompts for one AI coding session (Claude Code, Cursor, Windsurf or similar), plus a shared context block. Paste **Section B once at the start**, then paste **Prompt B1 → B6 one at a time**. Let each finish and run before sending the next.

Everything below matches the API contract your v0 frontend already expects (`lib/types.ts`, `lib/api.ts`) and the **real Gnani API** as documented at docs.gnani.ai (checked today).

---

## A. Gnani API facts the prompts rely on (verified against docs.gnani.ai)

| Item | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Prisma STT (REST)** | `POST https://api.vachana.ai/stt/v3`, multipart, header `X-API-Key-ID`. Fields: `audio_file`, `language_code` (required, e.g. `en-IN`, `ta-IN`), optional `model` (omit = Prisma v2.5 default, `prisma-v3.0` = v3). |
| **STT limits** | Formats: WAV, MP3, OGG, FLAC, AAC, M4A. **Max 30 seconds per request.** Browser `MediaRecorder` produces **WebM/Opus, which is not on the list.** Your frontend also allows 120 s answers. So the backend must **convert to WAV (16 kHz mono) and split into ≤28 s chunks**, then join the transcripts. |
| **STT response** | `{ success, request_id, transcript, model, ... }`. Empty transcript is not an error. Errors: `{success:false, error:{type,message}}` (400/500), gateway errors `{detail:{error_code,...}}` (401/403/429). |
| **Rate limit** | Some accounts allow **1 active request at a time** (429 `RATE_LIMITED`). The prompts serialize Gnani calls and retry with backoff. |
| **Timbre TTS (REST)** | `POST https://api.vachana.ai/api/v1/tts/inference`, JSON, header `X-API-Key-ID`. Body: `text`, `voice`, `model` (`timbre-v2.5`), `language`, `speed`, `audio_config {sample_rate, num_channels, sample_width, encoding:"linear_pcm", container:"wav"}`. Returns **raw binary audio**. |
| **Voices (Timbre v2.5)** | English `en-IN`: Kaveri, Trupti, Devika (female), Pranav, Shlok, Girish (male). Tamil `ta-IN`: Asmita, Trisha, Brinda, Vedika, Noopur. Voices are tied to a language, so use each voice with its own `language`. |
| **TTS input tip** | Numbers, dates and symbols should be written as spoken words, and markdown or code should be stripped before synthesis. |

Timbre v2.0 is being deprecated, so the prompts use **v2.5**.

